        12["<div style='font-weight: bold'>World Generation (infinite)</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Endless, chunked world:<br />terrain is a pure function of<br />(x, y, seed) via<br />valueNoise/fbm octaves,<br />streamed in lazily in 16x16<br />chunks and LRU-cached, so<br />there are no bounds, edges or<br />wrapping. Tile types (T) and<br />resource richness (rich/max,<br />uniformly random with no<br />distance ramp) are generated<br />per chunk; sparse per-tile<br />edits (mods) and per-chunk<br />fog bitmasks (explored) live<br />outside the cache so they<br />persist. FindSpawn picks a<br />random walkable birth tile<br />near (0,0); nothing is<br />sculpted.</div>"]
        style 12 fill:#3f7d3a,stroke:#2c5728,color:#ffffff
        13["<div style='font-weight: bold'>State and Saves</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>createState() builds the<br />canonical state object;<br />serialize/deserialize convert<br />it to a JSON save (format v3:<br />sparse richness deltas +<br />per-chunk fog bitmasks; older<br />v1/v2 saves are intentionally<br />discarded and the world<br />starts fresh). state.events<br />is transient and NEVER<br />serialized.</div>"]
        style 13 fill:#3f7d3a,stroke:#2c5728,color:#ffffff
        14["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Simulation Step</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>step(s, dt) - the heart of<br />the tick: extractor<br />production into buffers,<br />range-limited logistics<br />auto-collect, abundance<br />trickle, world regrowth<br />(REGROW_INTERVAL 0.5s, only<br />tiles near the player), time<br />+ stats. Called once per<br />frame by the app and by every<br />test.</div>"]
        style 14 fill:#3f7d3a,stroke:#2c5728,color:#ffffff
        15["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Gathering and Collection</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Manual actions: gather() from<br />a tile within GATHER_RANGE<br />(1.65) using axe/pickaxe<br />multipliers; collect() drains<br />extractor buffers within<br />COLLECT_RANGE (1.7).<br />gatherTarget/collectTarget<br />report what is actionable for<br />the UI.</div>"]
